    "prompt": "Create a painted 2D game animation sprite sheet for an original Runeterra Voidgrub adaptation, matching the compact textured pixel-painting appearance of Heroes of Might and Magic III creatures. Transparent background. No 3D render, plastic surface, photorealism, vector outline or splash-art effects. Exactly 16 separate whole-body poses in a STRICT 4 columns by 4 rows grid, equal cells, ample empty transparent gutters; no text, numbering, borders or ground planes. SAME creature, SAME scale, upper-left lighting and fixed low three-quarter battlefield view in every cell, generally faces screen RIGHT. Creature: squat purple segmented grub, hunched tough dark-violet chitin ridges, one short curved amber forehead horn, paired large pink eyes, a wide toothy dark maw, three small magenta membrane sacs on back, short tapering segmented tail, six short articulated prolegs under the belly; no wings, no clothes, no weapons. This project's creature physically crawls on prolegs, a grounded adaptation rather than floating. Restrained magenta highlights. Anatomy and proportions consistent, no duplication or missing limbs. Row1: neutral holding; slight breathing belly expansion; eyes/head alert raise; antenna/horn tilt idle. Row2 first2 and row3 all4 form a SIX FRAME alternating crawling cycle, whole body stays about same place; near and far prolegs genuinely trade planted support and lifted recovery, belly flexes subtly, no running leap. Row2 col3: flinch backward; row2 col4: brace crouched defense. Row4: right-facing start of turn; quarter-turned toward viewer; three-quarter turned toward viewer; final right-facing recovery. Every pose fits cell and keeps complete horn/tail/feet intact. Creature height around half cell, width about two thirds, generous blank gaps.\n",
